diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 20fdc15..1856633 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,86 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Preserve guest state in diagnostics when interpreting an unknown jump fails
+  decoding, and stop partial interpreter faults in STRICT_UNKNOWN mode before
+  fabricating a zero result or restoring the caller stack.
+
+- Render a bounded unlit/prelit Direct3D 9 fixed-function subset using real
+  FVF declarations and synthesized SM2 shaders shared by the CPU and GPU
+  paths. Refuse unsupported lighting, fog and texture stages explicitly;
+  preserve programmable bindings/constants and correct CPU point/clamp
+  sampling and DX9 pixel centres. Verify COM draws and offscreen Wasm pixels.
+
+- Add a real generated-code headless PE startup probe with verified local image
+  loading, strict import refusal and opt-in live guest snapshots at strict halts.
+
+- Add an opt-in STRICT_UNKNOWN runtime mode that stops at untranslated
+  calls or failed interpreted execution, retaining live instruction bytes
+  and decoder diagnostics instead of continuing with a zero result.
+
+- Execute PUSHFD/POPFD image trampolines and x87 real-memory load/store and
+  arithmetic forms in the fallback interpreter using the translated CPU's
+  flag, stack, tag and rounding model.
+
+- Implement InitializeCriticalSectionAndSpinCount through the recursive guest
+  lock scheduler and IsProcessorFeaturePresent using the guest CPU contract,
+  with registered stdcall argument counts for dynamic CRT startup calls.
+- Add a diagnostic mode for all generated chunks that keeps backend register
+  allocation without expensive LLVM IR optimization, preserving the normal
+  optimization level of native runtime sources.
+
+- Make guest cursor snapshots optional when a game's mouse object hooks are
+  absent; keep ordinary window and DirectInput motion without borrowing
+  another game's cursor layout.
+- Allow explicitly selected generated chunks to compile at O1 for diagnostic
+  builds, preserving the normal optimization level of every other source.
+- Allow the native formatter to select first-party paths without reformatting
+  unrelated local work.
+
+- Gate game-specific frame-clock substitutions on all configured hook
+  addresses; games without them compile and retain ordinary host-clock reads.
+- Bound computed MOV-immediate/NOP/JMP-register targets only with original
+  bytes and no intervening entry; unknown reachable jumps invalidate opaque
+  branch proofs, while unreachable ones do not invent entry points.
+- Read file offsets from 32-bit guest OVERLAPPED structures, preserve the
+  appropriate handle position, publish status/count/event completion, and
+  implement GetOverlappedResult for completed reads. Complete host reads
+  before returning pending async requests; reject unsupported blocking
+  pending states explicitly. Overlapped writes are not implemented here.
+- Route INT3/INT 3 through the existing fatal breakpoint handler, instead of
+  the ignored generic interrupt hook; SEH breakpoint continuation is not modeled.
+- During recursive recovery, skip only locally proven XOR-self/JE/JNE edges;
+  revisit a conditional if another edge enters it with unknown flags.
+- Publish resumable CALL returns from reachable sites and propagate newly
+  introduced entries to a fixed point; omit proven-dead CALL return markers.
+- Avoid reparsing non-FS operands in SEH scans and reuse each scan's branch
+  target set without changing the chain-head checks.
+- Prove original adjacent XOR-reg-self/JE/JNE branches only with no alternate
+  branch entry or computed jump; retain XOR writes and flags, and remove
+  only CFG paths the proven branch makes unreachable. Preserve taken edges
+  at conditional listing gaps as well as their fallthrough edges.
+- Translate 32-bit ENTER frame construction with nested frame copies,
+  five-bit nesting levels and unchanged arithmetic flags; keep 16-bit ENTER
+  explicitly unsupported pending a reliable differential stack oracle.
+- Recover LOOP taken paths and translate ZF-dependent loop aliases plus JCXZ;
+  respect CX address-size overrides and preserve flags and upper ECX bits.
+- Support same-descriptor segment POPs in the fixed flat Win32 context, with
+  correct stack operand widths; reject descriptor changes and SS single-step
+  states explicitly rather than silently ignoring them.
+- Index the union of decoded table storage ranges during code-pointer scans;
+  preserve covered-entry priority and exclusive interval ends.
+- Accept audited per-call nonlocal dispatcher transfers in resumable-stack
+  translations; preserve original CALL execution and trap unexpected fallthrough.
+- Index normalized declared data/code intervals for large annotated corpora.
+
+- Translate FEMMS with the defined MMX-exit tag effects shared with EMMS.
+
+- Let game translation inputs classify audited embedded PE file buffers as data;
+  retain their bytes and omit their listings and pointer-scan roots.
+
+- Cache immutable instruction decoding across overlapping static recovery walks;
+  preserve caller-specific bounds and return independent instruction objects.
+
 - Allow native game adapters to place their own cursors at absolute touch
   positions in logical game pixels. Placement can discard pending DirectInput
   X/Y movement without losing button, wheel or keyboard input.
