+`startup_win32_tests` exercises CRT critical-section and processor-feature
+imports through the real registry and dispatcher without an image or window.
+It checks dynamic resolution, stdcall stack cleanup, recursive ownership and
+the guest CPU feature contract. Its Emscripten build runs under Node.
+
+`game_boot_probe` links the real generated executable and auxiliary modules,
+then calls the verified PE entry through `run_entry` with the scheduler and
+actual import adapters. Its null graphics/audio host makes this a CPU startup
+diagnostic, not browser rendering or gameplay acceptance. Build the target
+through `tools/build.py`'s build API for the selected game. For Emscripten, run
+`node <output>/game_boot_probe.js <verified-executable>`; NODERAWFS reads the
+local installation and the loader still verifies every configured image hash.
+Both `RECOMP_STRICT_UNKNOWN` and `RECOMP_STRICT_IMPORTS` are forced on, so missing
+code, missing import implementations or unknown import signatures stop the run.
+Use an external execution timeout. `RECOMP_PROBE_DUMP=<existing-dir>/halt` writes
+live main/auxiliary images, stack, TEB and register metadata before a strict
+halt. These private diagnostic binaries belong under ignored `build/`.
+Decoder refusals also invoke the snapshot hook before executing instructions.
+`interp_tests --strict-fault` is an expected-abort check: a decoded routine
+pushes two stack words before an invalid memory read, and strict mode must
+retain that fault state rather than manufacture a successful zero return.
+
